              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When you're searching for a dry van trailer for sale, you're not just buying equipment; you're making a long-term investment in your fleet's reliability, uptime, and profitability. Whether you run a small operation or manage a growing fleet, the right dry van trailer can directly impact delivery schedules, maintenance costs, and overall ROI.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, we work with owner-operators and fleet managers across Florida who want straightforward guidance, dependable equipment, and a dealership relationship they can trust. This guide walks through what actually matters when sourcing a dry van trailer, so you can make a confident decision without the runaround.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-staple",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Dry Van Trailers Remain a Fleet Staple",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "staple"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-staple-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Dry van trailers continue to dominate freight hauling for a reason. They account for the majority of North American freight movement due to their versatility and cost efficiency. Their enclosed design protects cargo from weather, theft, and damage, making them ideal for retail goods, packaged food, manufacturing materials, and more. For Florida-based fleets, especially those operating in and around Tampa, dry vans offer flexibility across regional and long-haul routes without specialized equipment requirements.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/how-to-source-reliable-dry-van-trailers-for-sale/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Sun State technician inspecting the interior wall of a dry van trailer with a clipboard"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-what-to-look-for",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "What to Look for When Buying a Dry Van Trailer for Sale",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "what-to-look-for"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-what-to-look-for-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Not all dry van trailers are built or maintained the same. Before purchasing, focus on these key factors:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-what-to-look-for-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "type",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Build Quality and Materials",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Look for corrosion-resistant components, reinforced floors, and solid rear-door construction. Florida's heat and humidity demand trailers that can hold up long-term."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Manufacturer Reputation",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Proven manufacturers with strong engineering standards often deliver better longevity and resale value. A reputable trailer dealer should be transparent about where each unit comes from and how it's built."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Trailer Age and Condition",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "For new and used dry vans, condition matters more than mileage alone. A used trailer can deliver excellent ROI when sourced through a trusted dealer."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Warranty Coverage",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "A solid warranty protects your investment and reduces unexpected repair costs. New trailers typically offer the most comprehensive coverage, but select used units may still qualify for limited warranties."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-new-vs-used",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "New vs. Used Dry Van Trailers: Which Makes Sense for Your Fleet?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "new-vs-used"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-new-vs-used-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Choosing between new and used dry van trailers depends on your operating goals, budget, and growth timeline.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-new-vs-used-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "type",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "New Dry Van Trailers",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Latest engineering and materials"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Full manufacturer warranties"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Longer service life"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Ideal for growing fleets and long-term planning"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Used Dry Van Trailers",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Lower upfront cost"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Faster availability"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Strong ROI when properly maintained"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Ideal for owner-operators or supplemental fleet needs"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-new-vs-used-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At Sun State Trailers, we help customers evaluate both options honestly, because the \"best\" choice is the one that supports your business goals, not just the sale.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
